  "why": {
    "tokens": [
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "Reporting the last operation complete records the quantity produced and, depending on a parameter, posts it to inventory silently, not at all, or after asking. The order becomes "
      },
      {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Production Completed"
      },
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " when reported and "
      },
      {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Completed"
      },
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " only when Warehousing finishes the inbound receipt, so the two statuses are a handoff, not a failure. The phase ends with an inventory read because the Manufacturing-side status alone does not prove the stock arrived."
      }
    ],
